-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party software NOT redistributed here
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository vendors no third-party source. The items below are fetched,
built, or downloaded on the user's or the build machine's own terms. Where a
published release artifact carries third-party binaries, the entry says so.

llama.cpp (MIT License)
    https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
    The native worker in unridden/api/native is compiled against a llama.cpp
    checkout that the user provides at a pinned revision. Its headers, its
    bundled nlohmann/json, and its examples/gguf-hash/deps/sha256 helper are
    read from that checkout at build time. No llama.cpp or ggml file is copied
    into this repository and none is distributed with it. The MIT license text
    ships with llama.cpp itself.

NVIDIA CUDA runtime libraries (NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit EULA)
    https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/
    No CUDA file is in this repository. A CUDA build of the base runtime copies
    libcudart, libcublas and libcublasLt out of the CUDA toolkit already on the
    build machine and into the worker bundle, so that running the result needs
    only the NVIDIA driver. The prebuilt CUDA bundles this project publishes on
    GitHub Releases therefore contain those NVIDIA redistributable libraries,
    under NVIDIA's terms rather than this project's Apache-2.0 licence.
    `build_base_runtime.py --no-cuda-redist` builds without them.

Gemma model weights (Gemma Terms of Use)
    No model weights are included, mirrored, or redistributed here. The user
    downloads the GGUF they want and accepts Google's Gemma Terms of Use and
    Prohibited Use Policy directly.

